 const methodTheory={gauss:["Gauss–Jordan elimination","[A | b] → [I | x]","A square system Ax = b has a unique solution if A is nonsingular.","Partial pivoting reduces some rounding problems but cannot eliminate ill-conditioning."],jacobi:["Jacobi iteration","xᵢ⁽ᵏ⁺¹⁾ = (bᵢ − Σⱼ≠ᵢ aᵢⱼxⱼ⁽ᵏ⁾) / aᵢᵢ","All diagonal entries must be nonzero. Strict row diagonal dominance is a sufficient, not necessary, convergence condition."],seidel:["Gauss–Seidel iteration","xᵢ⁽ᵏ⁺¹⁾ = (bᵢ − Σⱼ<ᵢ aᵢⱼxⱼ⁽ᵏ⁺¹⁾ − Σⱼ>ᵢ aᵢⱼxⱼ⁽ᵏ⁾) / aᵢᵢ","Strict row diagonal dominance or symmetric positive definiteness is sufficient for convergence."],det:["Determinant","det(A) = (−1)ˢ ∏ᵢ pᵢ","The determinant is defined for every square matrix, including singular matrices.","Partial pivoting tracks row swaps and pivot products; numerical rank is tolerance-dependent."],inverse:["Inverse matrix","[A | I] → [I | A⁻¹]","An inverse exists exactly when a square matrix is nonsingular. Near-singular matrices can have inaccurate inverses."],krylov:["Krylov / Arnoldi–QR","Kₘ(A,v) = span(v, Av, …, Aᵐ⁻¹v)","The implementation uses restarted orthogonal Krylov chains and shifted QR. A single cyclic vector is not required.","Repeated eigenvalues need not have a complete eigenvector basis."],lagrange:["Lagrange interpolation","L(x) = Σᵢ yᵢ ∏ⱼ≠ᵢ (x − xⱼ)/(xᵢ − xⱼ)","Distinct x nodes define a unique polynomial of degree at most n − 1. Extrapolation and high-degree interpolation may be unreliable."],sweep:["Sweep method (Thomas algorithm)","lᵢyᵢ₋₁ + dᵢyᵢ + uᵢyᵢ₊₁ = rᵢ","The discretized tridiagonal system must admit nonzero sweep pivots. Boundary derivatives use first-order one-sided differences."],newton:["Newton method","xₖ₊₁ = xₖ − f(xₖ)/f′(xₖ)","Newton convergence depends on the initial guess, smoothness and a nonzero derivative near a simple root.","Stop when both the absolute step and the residual satisfy their respective tolerances. A small residual alone does not bound root error."],fixed:["Fixed-point iteration","xₖ₊₁ = g(xₖ)","For a convergence guarantee on an interval, g must map the interval into itself and satisfy |g′(x)| ≤ q < 1 throughout it.","The derivative at the computed point is only a local diagnostic, not an interval-wide proof."],trap:["Trapezoidal rule","Iₙ = h[f(a)/2 + Σᵢ₌₁ⁿ⁻¹ f(a + ih) + f(b)/2]","For sufficiently smooth f, the composite trapezoidal rule has order p = 2.","Use a positive target error to refine the grid automatically, or enter 0 to retain the requested grid."],simpson:["Simpson's rule","Iₙ = (h/3)[f(x₀) + 4f(x₁) + 2f(x₂) + … + f(xₙ)]","For sufficiently smooth f, the composite Simpson rule has order p = 4 and requires even n.","Use a positive target error to refine the grid automatically, or enter 0 to retain the requested grid."]};

